@startuml state-seat-flight
title Seat Hold + FlightSchedule Lifecycles (Iteration 3 additions)
hide empty description
skinparam stateFontSize 12
skinparam ranksep 55
skinparam nodesep 40
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 130

state "Seat lifecycle" as SeatSL {
  [*] -down-> Available
  Available -right-> Held : hold()
  Held -down-> Reserved : reserve()
  Held -left-> Available : release / sweep
  Reserved -up-> Available : release()
}

state "FlightSchedule lifecycle" as FsSL {
  [*] -down-> Scheduled
  Scheduled -up-> Delayed : DELAYED
  Delayed -down-> Scheduled : SCHEDULED
  Scheduled -right-> Cancelled : CANCELLED
  Delayed -right-> Cancelled : CANCELLED
  Cancelled -down-> [*]
}

note bottom of SeatSL
  Iter3 additions:
   - hold(timeout, pnr) starts the 15-minute timer
   - sweep() detects Seat.isHoldExpired() and publishes
     SeatHoldExpiredEvent (ReservationHoldListener cascades)
end note

note bottom of FsSL
  Iter3 additions:
   - Transition method = changeStatus(newStatus)
   - Every changeStatus() publishes FlightStatusChangedEvent
   - AffectedReservationListener walks ReservationRegistry
end note
@enduml
